year":"2026 so far: 34 daily record highs, 3 daily record lows","records":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","change":"Lakeland's days and nights both warmed. Days warmed faster.","rain":"Lakeland has gotten wetter"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 77\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>77\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 79\u00b0F, and the record is 93\u00b0F (1986). The low of <strong>64\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Lakeland's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Lakeland has set <strong>121 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 125 that chance alone would give, and <strong>150 record highs</strong>, close to the 125 that chance alone would give. The 1980s hold the most record highs of any decade (116). Lakeland's all-time high is 105\u00b0F, on June 4, 1985.","t_chg":"Lakeland's days and nights both warmed. Days warmed faster.","p_chg":"Across 75 complete years: Lakeland's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.21\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.08 to +0.34), about +1.6\u00b0F since 1949. Lakeland's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.62\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.49 to +0.75), about +4.7\u00b0F since 1949.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 4 of 12 months. Highs rose in all 12 months.","t_rain":"Lakeland has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Lakeland's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+1.64 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.68 to +2.60), about +12.5 inches since 1949. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 56.9 inches a year. The wettest year was 2018 (78.15 in); the driest, 1961 (35.83 in). Lakeland almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 34 daily record highs, 3 daily record lows"}}